properties.summary:
getting-started/skills/capture-intent/SKILL.md, with its .claude and .grok mirrors byte-identical, gains one paragraph after "Search before you add". Before a structural addition (a new requirement, capability, component, rule or step), ask the person whether something could be removed in its place, or whether the addition lets something go, and write the answer down. The rest of the paragraph:
- ask it on structural additions only, never on a wording, a fix or a status;
- take away from what is built, required or ruled, newest and least proven first;
- never take away from the record;
- it is a question, not a gate.
The skill names no node id, because it is served to every design and the rule's id exists only in reflow2's. Checks: skill_lint and its tests pass, test_init 132 OK (no install golden carries the skill body), and served_skills.rs 15 pass.
